# Snyk

> Snyk, the AI security company, secures software created by developers and AI across application code, open source dependencies, container images, infrastructure as code, APIs, and web applications, AI-assisted development, and AI-native and agentic applications. The Snyk AI Security Platform delivers the AI Security Fabric: continuous, autonomous defense woven across the software development lifecycle, so organizations can trust AI to innovate without limits.

This file is a curated map of Snyk's public platform, product, documentation, and reference pages. Use the platform, engine, and solution pages to understand capabilities and product selection. Use the documentation links for setup, supported technologies, APIs, integrations, and current product behavior. Use the content hubs and downloadable resources for research, data, reports, and practical guidance.

## Platform and AI security

- [Snyk AI Security Platform](https://snyk.io/platform/): Overview of Snyk's application security and AI security capabilities. Use for the high-level platform and how its components fit together.
- [Evo by Snyk](https://snyk.io/evo/): Security and governance for agentic development and AI-native applications, spanning agentic development security, AI security posture management, and continuous offensive security. Use for Snyk's AI-agent and AI-application security capabilities.
- [Evo Agentic Development Security](https://snyk.io/evo/agentic-development-security/): Real-time enforcement across the agent development lifecycle — governing the tools agents use, the actions they take, and the code they generate. Use for securing AI coding agents, MCP servers, and agent skills.
- [Evo AI Security Posture Management (AI-SPM)](https://snyk.io/evo/aispm/): Visibility and governance of AI assets, models, and services across the enterprise. Use for AI inventory, posture, and AI-BOM questions.
- [Evo Continuous Offensive Security](https://snyk.io/evo/continuous-offensive-security/): Simulated attacks that surface exploitable vulnerabilities before adversaries do. Use for offensive testing and exploitability validation. Evo COS invokes on Snyk API & Web's dynamic testing engine and Snyk Code's static analysis.
- [DeepCode AI](https://snyk.io/platform/deepcode-ai/): Snyk's AI-assisted code analysis and fix technology. Use for questions about the analysis and remediation technology behind Snyk Code.
- [Integrations](https://snyk.io/integrations/): Supported source control, CI/CD, IDE, container, workflow, and AI-development integrations. Used to determine how Snyk connects to an existing toolchain.

## Security engines

- [Snyk Code](https://snyk.io/product/snyk-code/): Static application security testing for first-party source code. Use for questions about finding and fixing vulnerabilities in proprietary code.
- [Snyk Open Source](https://snyk.io/product/open-source-security-management/): Vulnerability and license analysis for open-source dependencies. Use for software composition analysis and dependency risk.
- [Snyk Container](https://snyk.io/product/container-vulnerability-management/): Vulnerability analysis for container images and workloads. Use for container and base-image security.
- [Snyk Infrastructure as Code](https://snyk.io/product/infrastructure-as-code-security/): Misconfiguration analysis for infrastructure-as-code files. Use for Terraform, Kubernetes, and cloud configuration security.
- [Snyk API & Web](https://snyk.io/product/dast-api-web/): Dynamic security testing for running APIs and web applications. Use for testing running APIs and web applications from the outside in (DAST / black-box testing).


## Solutions

- [Secure AI-generated code](https://snyk.io/solutions/secure-ai-generated-code/): Product and workflow overview for validating code produced by AI coding tools. Use when the topic is security for AI-assisted software development.
- [Secure at inception for AI](https://snyk.io/solutions/secure-at-inception-for-ai/): Embedding security into AI-driven and agentic development so new code is secure at the point of creation, powered by Snyk Studio, Snyk Code, and DeepCode AI. Use for the "secure at inception" approach to preventing insecure AI-generated code while clearing existing security debt.
- [Application security](https://snyk.io/solutions/application-security/): Snyk's AppSec program across the software development lifecycle. Use for broad application-security strategy and program questions.
- [Software supply chain security](https://snyk.io/solutions/software-supply-chain-security/): Security for dependencies, build workflows, software bills of materials, and supply-chain risk. Use for software supply chain questions.
- [Zero-day vulnerability security](https://snyk.io/solutions/zero-day-vulnerability-security/): Detection and rapid response for newly disclosed and zero-day vulnerabilities. Use for identifying and remediating emerging vulnerabilities across code and dependencies.
- [Risk-based prioritization](https://snyk.io/solutions/risk-based-prioritization/): Prioritization of findings by real risk, using context such as reachability and exploit maturity. Use for triaging and focusing remediation on what matters most.


